A stack's pages written under a `for` over a constant, under an `if` the
build decides, and in a group -- a component that renders pages without
being one -- on every target that answers a stack.

html writes a document per copy: the loop's two items are one/index.html and
index.html (the second's slug is empty, so it is the page at "/"), each with
the copy's own title, the `if`'s page is about/, the group's page is faq/, and
contact/ is the page the button goes to. A loop of pages is no render slot there, since each document holds
one copy and the loop is gone before anything renders.

android declares a destination per page, a copy's route holding which copy it
is and the destination binding the loop's variables back from it.

gtk4, fyne and bubbletea keep the loop: each copy of the page is the `if` on
the record's `id` and its `copy`, the iteration the record holds, so going to
one copy shows it and not its sibling. Where a copy may be the start, the
stack's first page is asked for by `pages__start`, which looks for the page at
"/" among the copies and falls back to the first page written. The group is
spliced into the stack before the pages are numbered, so its page is one like
any other.

deny out/none/html/index.html `<span>FAQ only</span>` -- a document holds its one page
deny out/none/html/one/index.html `globalThis.__sngl_page` -- a document reading no page at run time publishes none
deny * `extras` -- a group is spliced where it is written and reaches no backend

-- app.sngl --
import nav "sngl:ui/nav"
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
    go {
        gtk4
        fyne
        bubbletea
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

struct Item {
    slug string
    title string
}

const items list<Item> = [
    {slug="one", title="One"},
    {slug="", title="Two"},
]

const withAbout = true

component extras {
    nav.page #faq(href="/faq", title="FAQ") {
        ui.text(value="FAQ only")
    }
}

ui.window(title="Site - {pages.current.title}") {
    ui.vbox {
        nav.stack #pages {
            for var it = items {
                nav.page #item(href="/" + it.slug, title=it.title) {
                    ui.text(value=it.title)
                    ui.text(value=pages.current == item ? "showing" : "hidden")
                }
            }
            if withAbout {
                nav.page #about(href="/about", title="About") {
                    ui.text(value="about")
                }
            }
            extras
            nav.page #contact(href="/contact", title="Contact") {
                ui.text(value="contact")
            }
        }
        ui.button(text="Contact", @click { pages.go(contact) })
        ui.button(text="Back", @click { pages.back() })
    }
}
